kanatrain
=========

A mistake-driven hiragana and katakana trainer for the terminal.
Written in Rust, standard library only.

Install
-------

  cargo install kanatrain
  kanatrain

Make sure ~/.cargo/bin is in your PATH. To update later:

  cargo install kanatrain --force

Build and run from source
-------------------------

  cargo run --release

or

  cargo build --release
  ./target/release/kanatrain

Options
-------

  --reset      forget saved statistics
  --no-color   disable colors (NO_COLOR is also honoured)
  -h, --help   show usage

Modes
-----

  Script    hiragana, katakana, or both
  Sets      1  single kana        (a ka sa ...)
            2  voiced singles     (ga za pa ...)
            3  combined kana      (kya shu cho ...)
            w  weak spots only    (kana you have missed before)
  Length    number of questions, 0 for endless

Sets can be combined, e.g. "1 3".

Answering
---------

Type the romaji and press Enter.

  ?   show the answer (counts as a miss)
  q   finish the session

Common alternate spellings are accepted (si, tu, hu, tya, jya, di ...).

How it teaches
--------------

  - Kana you miss are asked more often. Weights persist between runs.
  - A missed kana returns a few questions later as a second chance.
  - After a miss you must type the correct reading once to move on.
  - Every miss prints a side-by-side comparison of what you typed and
    the correct answer, plus look-alike kana, and for combined kana a
    breakdown such as  ki + small ya -> kya.
  - The end-of-session report lists each mistake and what you typed
    instead, then your weakest kana overall.

Files
-----

  Stats are stored in $XDG_DATA_HOME/kanatrain/stats.tsv
  (default ~/.local/share/kanatrain/stats.tsv).

Not covered
-----------

  Extended katakana (ti, fa ...), long vowels, small tsu.

Development
-----------

  src/main.rs      argument handling and the round loop
  src/lib.rs       module list
  src/data.rs      kana tables, cards, look-alike groups
  src/feedback.rs  answer lookup and the comparison panel
  src/session.rs   menu, card selection and the quiz loop
  src/stats.rs     per-kana weights and persistence
  src/rng.rs       xorshift generator
  src/term.rs      colors, width and padding, prompting
  tests/cli.rs     end-to-end tests against the real binary

  cargo test
  cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
  cargo fmt --check
